# DESCEND Frontend UX Rules

- Single question layout: render exactly one question per screen.
- Progress bar anchored at the absolute top of the assessment screens.
- Typography: minimum base text 16px; headings 22px–28px.
- Color palette: page `#F0F8FF`, cards `#FFFFFF`, primary `#2E7D32`, text `#1F2937`. Use CSS variables from `index.css`.
- Touch targets: buttons and clickable areas at least 44×44px.
- Icons: lucide-react only. Never use emojis.
- Language: instant English / Tagalog toggle via shared language state.
- Medical framing: educational disclaimers in neutral gray containers. Avoid bright red for health warnings.
- Accessibility: Web Speech API for reading questions aloud.
- Stack: React, Vite, TypeScript with strict typing for survey factors.
